Is anyone here successfully using a "wheel mouse" on a Tru64 based 
workstation?

I use a KVM (keyboard, video, mouse) switch to share a single keyboard, 21" 
monitor and mouse between 3 computers at my desk.  This is a great savings 
in desktop space as well as money and it works great.  I have no problems 
when I use my 3-button Compaq mouse - it works equally well in Unix and 
Windows (with Windows ignoring the middle button, of course).

However, I'd like to use a new MS IntelliMouse Optical that I just picked 
up.  It works great in Windows and it works fine in Tru64 also, except that 
there doesn't seem to be a way to generate a "middle button click".  The 
wheel doesn't work either, but that is much less of a problem.

Has anybody been down this path already?  Any luck?

Thanks,

Mark

