Thanks to Phil Lawrence for the answer :

hwmgr -remove name -entry tu0
hwmgr -remove name -entry tu1
 
then reboot and the network device should pick up tu0

And indeed it did....shame about the requirement for a reboot - very
Windows'esque !!!

It was suggested to try dsfmgr -m tu1 0 but this only seems to work for SCSI
devices.

Regards

Kevin Jones

-----Original Message-----

Hello 

Having relocated a network card from one PCI slot to another, it now
appears as tu1 instead of tu0. 

Is there a way of renaming back to tu0 ? 

This is V5.1 patch kit 3. 

I've had a try with some of the hwmgr -set ....... and sysman -cli set
attr .... commands. But these imply that it cannot be renamed. The
trouble is that the hwmgr command is very cumbersome and it is very
difficult to work out the precise switches to enable you to do anything.

Regards 

Kevin Jones 



