add unit D91 CLONE1 disable_access_path=all
set D91 id=291
set D91 enable_access_path=BCK010-1,BCK010-2,BCK012-1,BCK012-2

Up to this point all is working well.

On the backup server (ES40 also running 5.1):
hwmgr -scan scsi 
hwmgr -view dev |grep IDENTIFIER=291
ln -s /dev/disk/dsk111c /etc/fdmns/prd_u01_domain
mount -t advfs -r prd_u01_domain#u01 /u01

At this point the mount command will sometimes "freeze up".  There are no 
errors returned and nothing in any of the logs to indicate the problem.  A 
process shows up "advfs -F  0x40000" in uninterruptable sleep.  Any advfs 
command run on this volume freezes up as well.  There is no apparent pattern to 
which domains will have this problem.  u01 will fail one time then work the 
next and the same for the other 13 domains.  We have tried this with the Oracle 
database up and in hot backup mode and down.

All domains are single lun mirror sets or striped mirror sets.  LSM is not in 
use. 

Any ideas?

TIA 
Allen

