the right direction if this question shouldn't be asked here. =20
I just got a cute little X-terminal to be used to connect to our Tru64 =
(5.1 patch 3) servers, and run our main production application.  I setup =
the terminal to use XDMCP, so we could choose which host to connect to =
at bootup.  The problem is that right now our production environment is =
split into 2 networks, and the terminal can only seem to connect via =
XDMCP to the servers on the same network.  It can ping, and telnet to =
ALL the servers--so there is connectivity.  I'm thinking it's the way =
XDMCP broadcasts over the network.  It's definitely not a problem with =
the terminal, because I setup Xcursion (NT PC) to use XDMCP and it came =
up with the same list of servers as the terminal.  So basically I was =
wondering if there is a way around this issue, or if someone could at =
least point me in the right direction.  TIA

