From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Oct 24 20:07:22 2001
From: "Kemp, Tom" <Tom.Kemp () dowjones ! com>
Date: Wed, 24 Oct 2001 20:07:22 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: WWIDMGR Summary (Changing a WWN on a KGPSA)
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653641822006

	Original Post:

> Is it possible to use the WWIDMGR change the WWID of a KGPSA-CA host bus
> adapter?  If so, does anyone have a procedure to do so?
> 
	The answer is "no", the WWIDMGR can not.  

	Information provided by our VAR has shown us, via a procedure, where
the emulex LP6DUTIL tool can change the WWN on a KGPSA.  Here is a link to
the Emulex site, the guys who actually make the board, and their own
procedure.  

	
http://www.emulex.com/expsearch/clearexp_cgi/solution.htm?probdesc.objid=268
438284 

	The text from the site:

	Here's the writeup on how to correctly change IEEE addresses and
Node A 
	Config parameters. 

	As to what procedure should be used to work around this problem when
using 
	LP6DUTIL it depends on exactly what value you are trying to change.
Several 
	parameters are stored in the Flash. 

	1. Permenant IEEE (World Wide Port Name) that is the same as the
IEEE 
	Address that is on a bar code label on the board. 

	If you are trying to change the permenant IEEE Address (the one that
is on 
	the board tag) you should use the following procedure 

	1. From the Main Menu Enter 5 to get to Maintenance Menu 
	2. From the Maintenance Menu Enter C to get to the Update Config
Menu. 
	3. From the Update Config Menu Enter C again 
	4. When prompted enter desired values for the IEEE Address and be
returned 
	to the Update Config Data Menu. Enter 0 to return to the Main Menu. 
	5. Enter 3 to restart the card. 

	This procedure will change only the permanent IEEE address stored in
region 
	F of the Flash and has no effect on the Node or Port Name stored in
region 0 
	or the Preferred D_ID or Hard AL_PA also stored in region 0. 

	2. User configurable Port_Name or Node_Name, whose default value
coming out 
	of the factory is derived from the permanent IEEE address 

	If you are trying to change the user configurable Node_Name or
Port_Name you 
	should use the following procedure. 

	1. From the Main Menu Enter 5 to get to Maintenance Menu 
	2. From the Maintenance Menu Enter C to get to the Update Config
Menu. 
	3. From the Update Config Menu Enter 1 to configure Node A 
	4. When prompted enter desired values or accept default for the
Port_Name 
	and Node_Name 
	5. When prompted for the Preferred D_ID do not accept the 
	default but instead Enter 0. 
	6. When prompted for Hard AL_PA do not accept the 
	default but instead Enter 0 or required value. 
	7. Enter 0 to return to the Main Menu and Enter 3 to restart the
card. 

	This procedure will only change the parameters stored in region 0 of
the 
	Flash and has no effect on the permanent IEEE address stored in
region F of 
	the Flash. 

	We have not tried our VAR's procedure or Emulex's, so use the tool
at your own risk. 

	Steps to run the tool:

	P00>>>
	ARC -> Utilities -> Run program -> A: ALPHDNLD.EXE


	Thanks.

	T. Kemp

