Hi,

The consensus seemed to be that saving the configuration wasn't needed
when you have redundant controllers, since the configuration is stored
on both controllers.  I guess you just have to type the configuration
in again if you have some sort of disaster that requires replacing
both controllers. The documentation for CONFIG SAVE specifically states:

"This command is appropriate only for a single-controller sub-system."

Thanks to all who replied.
-- 
