Orig Post: Trying to find out upgrade options for AS2000
 
Thanks to Alan for his succinct response...
-------------------------------------------------------------------
The April 1998 Systems and Options Catalog listed the
following (relevant) AlphaServer 2000 CPU upgrade:
4/200,4/233 -> 4/275
4/200,4/233,4/275 -> 5/250
4/200,4/233,4/275 -> 5/300
4/200,4/233 -> 5/375
Maximium memory is indeed 1 GB, spread over two slots.
Given the amount you have it seems likely that you could
get another 512 MB module to upgrade to the maximum.
There might also be some I/O options available. The
DE500 (10/100 Ethernet) and KZPBA (UltraFast/Wide SCSI)
are supported. The KZPBA might allow faster and more
storage..
----------------------------------------------------------------


