Well,
Thanks to all who replied.
I just killed the decterm (dtwm) process that was running on the console
and it logged me off the console, then I logged in again without any 
problems.
Though I didn't try any of the suggested remedies, I will sure try them 
when it happens again, or I will force the problem to happen then try 
to solve it on a test machine.
Thanx ALL
Here are some of the interesting replies I got

----------------------------------------------
>From Stan Horwitz:
I do not know if this is related to your problem, but have you seen the
recent CERT advisory about a buffer overflow vulnerability with CDE's
ToolTalk? If not, you certainly should. The advisory is available at
http://www.cert.org/advisories/CA-2001-27.html
-------------------------------------------------
>From True64 User:
I kept getting this message about ttdb.serverd cannot
connect, tooltalk may not be running. So, i tested it
by disabling ttdb in /etc/inetd.conf
>From there I encountered the symptoms u have, so I
re-enabled ttdb (tool talk db server).
----------------------------------------------------
>From Ayman Rayyan:
Try to remove the ( .TTauthoriuty ) file from root home directory.




