Akbarzadeh, Saeid sent the following indented text:
> 
> Hello, Does anyone know what are some of the reasons why our SMTP mails
> doest not get routed from Unix.

It may be that relaying has been blocked.  Allowing indiscriminant
relaying means that spammers can use your box for spamming; as a
consequence, most have relaying from unknown locations blocked.

I would look in your 'sendmail.cf' file and look for rules which
produce a "Relay denied" error.

Hope th^s helps!

John

