Hello everyone,

In my WS500au I have a Digital 4D10T Graphics card.  After installing 5.1
(and firmware 5.8) I can not get the Xserver started.  It basically
coredumps and crashes the system.  After a couple of failed attempts, I
figured I would go aheard and install an older version Tru64/DIGITAL
to see if it could be the card was no longer supported; thus I installed
4.0E.  During the install of the packages it informs me that it has detected
a new graphics controller and will install the required packages.  
Once this is done the system boots. After the boot process and during the
kernel loading process, it comes up with:
  Comet0 at bus 0 slot 11
  This system requires a driver for it's video card. 
  Enter the device where the kit can be found (e.g. rz4c).
(on the next boot, in place of the above it will say:   dli configured  )
So...  I used rz16a rz16b ( / and /usr)    I've also used the device names
for the CDROM.   And still I get a core dump (but does not crash under
4.0E).

Any Ideas?   suggestions?  Should I get a new graphics card?



-Will

