From: Peter.Stern () weizmann ! ac ! il
Date: Fri, 19 Oct 2001 11:10:18 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: FRU Table
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653641821914

I got a very quick reply to this query from Andrew Mitcham for which I
thank him.

His answer and my query are provided below.

> 
> **ERROR svrsys_fru_parse.c line 1031: FRU Table revision 5.2
>         is not supported.
> 
> 
> The message is being generated by DECEVENT and can be ignored.
> DECEVENT will not run on EV6 systems. The FRU table is something
> provided by the console firmware. It would appear that this error is
> referring to the FRU table that the console builds and passes to the
> kernel
> at boot time. The error message is from the svrSystem_mib subagent.
> 
> 
> There is a release note explaining the svrMgt_mib and svrSystem_mib
> Subagents. The thMIB definitions are in /usr/share/sysman/mibs. The
> documentation is within the MIB files themselves. Currently, the MIBs
> are not configured for EV6 platforms. There has been a lot of confusion
> about these messages. In a future release, they will be
> addressed/suppressed.
> 
>  Q. Why do these error messages appear at all?
>  A. There is a mismatch in the firmware and the operating system that
>     checks The FRU table. T his will be corrected in a future version
>     of the OS /  Firmware. T he message has no affect with the operation
>     of your system.
> 
> 
>  Q. What daemon causes the error message?
>  A. envmon:SVRSYSMIB=/usr/sbin/svrSystem_mib
>     snmpd:SVRSYSMIB=/usr/sbin/svrSystem_mib
> 
> 
> 
