I've got an interim fix for this. I believe the problem to be network 
related though I haven't defined exactly what is. Suspects are the onboard 
tu interface or perhaps a failing switch. The ASU software was configured to 
use the primary gigabit interface alt0 with some NETBIOS traffic running 
over tu0. tu0 showed some errors in netstat so I've removed it from the ASU 
config. The problems experienced by the PC client users have stopped. Note 
that the print problems were restricted to PC application users. Unix lpd 
print users who by default would use the alt0 interface weren't affected. 
I've zeroed the stats on tu0 and even after a short time the error count is 
significant.

There are some other network oddities on site so I'm inclined to think the 
fault lies with one of the switches.

Thanks go to Jan Hansen and especially to William Skulley for their 
assistance.


Joe


