is an installation for Powerstorm - I installed this and the description on
the installation was Powerstorm 3D - OpenGL installation.  Once I installed
this, I was okay.  Thanks for all the help.


From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Oct 16 16:48:31 2001
From: tsh () mrc-lmb ! cam ! ac ! uk
Date: Tue, 16 Oct 2001 16:48:31 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: TLZ10-VA dipsw settings
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653641821850




Thanks everyone, it seems its all in the part-number.
A TLZ10-VA is a narrow-SCSI device. The VA says it all.
If it was wide SCSI, it would be a TLZ10-VW.

However, the quickspec at 

http://www.compaq.com/products/quickspecs/10239_div/10239_div.html

says that the 12/24Gb-family DAT drives are Fast-wide/Single-ended
and only offers a DS-TLZ10-VA part in the SBB format.....

Such is life.

Cheers,
Terry.

