To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY Rebuild sendmail/bind after patch kit install?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653641821757

Hello Sys Admins,

I received one reply directly addressing my question.
Thanks to Steve VanDevender for his information.  He has not found
it necessary to rebuild stuff after upgrading to the latest patch 
kit, as long as he took the required steps to preserve his locally-
built versions from being overwritten.

I was worried that previously compiled binaries of local versions 
of sendmail and bind would fail to work correctly (maybe in very
subtle ways) after a patch upgrade, forcing me to re-build those 
apps from scratch.  Thanks very much for your input, Steve.

Paul Youngblood

---------original  posting  follows------------------------------

> Hello system admins,
> 
> I'm running recent versions of sendmail and DNS(bind) on Tru64 v4.0F
> (patch kit #4), and I want to apply patch kit #6.  Should I plan on
> rebuilding/reinstalling sendmail and bind after I apply the patch
> kit?  Or, is it enough to just temporarily move the necessary sendmail
> and bind binaries and config files, and then move them back after the
> patch kit installation? 
> 
> Paul Youngblood
> youngbp@uahis1.uah.edu
