On Fri, 5 Oct 2001, Lucio Chiappetti wrote:

> Yesterday, after a day of intensive use, suddenly the CD does not work an=
y
> more. When I try the usual mount [it gives]

> /dev/rz4c on /cdrom: No such device or address
>
> But the device files are all there !
> Also there are no SCSI CAM errors in the uerf log

Thanks to alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com and Antonio Gonz=E1lez for pointing out
that the "No such device or address" has nothing to do with device files
but indicates a communication error.

They also pointed me out the command "scu" with an extensive man page, and
the use of some commands. I tried among other the following

scu> show device
scu> tur                                             (test unit ready)
scu> test                                            (self test)
scu> read media starting 0 ending 100 compare off    (read test)

The first works even with no CD in the caddy, the other require a CD.
Apparently they all work, and now I am able again to mount my CD !!

Glad to find there is no hardware problem !

