Subject: Summary RA3000 Serial Port Connection
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653641821592


Thanks for all of the responses.

The question was " How do I get the serial port of the RA3000 to work
in a character cell mode, after accessing it with the SWCC software?" The
answer is that the serial port in character cell mode is not a supported
method of managing the RA3000 or it's raid sets. However, entering "escape
shift 7" will place the port into a menu mode that can be used for some
basic management functions.

There is a password (decraid) that may be required in order to access this
menu.

Again, thanks to Compaq support and several other respondents.


John F. Harvey

