thanks to Jan Mark Holzer@DEC, i have an answer:
===========
if you have installed the TruCluster subsets and have been running
Production Server your 
    only option to remove the MC hardware and run the traditional ASE
software is to
    re-install the cluster subsets.
    As the asecdb does include/"remember" cluster specific information
(including
    MC) you'll have to re-init the asecdb as well.
    As of 1.6 we do support the usage of description files for services
which should
    at least configuring the services somewhat easier.
 
Hth,
 
    Jan
=========
 
so, delete trucluster subsets --> remove MC hardware --> reinstall
trucluster subsets and setup ASE again w/ new asecdb.
 
--Brandon
 
-----Original Message-----
From: Brandon Smith [mailto:brandon.smith@totaltec.com]
Sent: Monday, October 01, 2001 6:11 PM
To: tru64-unix-managers@ornl.gov
