Operational: There are insufficient configuration copies in disk group
rootdg ( 3 ). 
You must increase the number of configuration copies by adding more disks or
by re-adding disks that have active configuration areas. Check each disk in
voldg list rootdg. To correct the problem, use the following command,
setting privlen, nconfig, and nlog the same for all disks: 
voldisksetup -i diskname privlen=nnn, nconfig=n nlog=n
Add the disk to LSM: 
voldg -g rootdg adddisk diskname

Operational: There is an insufficient number of log copies in disk group
rootdg ( 3 ). 
You must increase the number of log copies by adding more disks or by
re-adding disks with active configuration areas. Check each disk in voldg
list rootdg. To correct the problem, use the following command, setting
privlen, nconfig, and nlog the same on all disks: 
voldisksetup -i diskname privlen=nnn, nconfig=n nlog=n
Add the disk to LSM: 
voldg -g rootdg adddisk diskname

Trying to list rootdg gives the following error :-

[canada]/tmp $ voldisk list rootdg
lsm:voldisk: ERROR: Disk rootdg: Disk not in the configuration

Can anyone explain what iscausing this and what corrective action is
required ?

Regards,
Mike.



