From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Oct 09 18:08:03 2001
From: Andy Cohen <Andy.Cohen () cognex ! com>
Date: Tue, 09 Oct 2001 18:08:03 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: 'System corrected errors' in messages file
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653641821701

Thanks to all for helping with this.  Bottom line was a bad disk.  Answers
ranged from 'transient errors' to 'call Compaq'.  I did call Compaq Service
who reviewed the binary.errlog and determined a problem with memory in one
of two slots.  Field service replaced one, reseated the other and the
problem seems to have been fixed.

One particularly interesting comment:

Are all your memory cards the same size?

I get this message on one of my boxes after replacing hardware and long
calls w/ Compaq/digital the rep realized that there is a 'shell game' that
the firmware pulls on the hardware.  This shell game only happens when the
memory cards are of different sizes.


Note: We found out that Compaq Analyze 2.1 seems to read a samples file:

the older version of CA ver2.10 is the problem or has the feature 
where if you do #ca analyze    it runs out to the CA examples directory
and runs against the sample binary.errlog files  not the real node=ODIN
binary.errlog....

suggestion is to get you to install the new version CA ver3.1 and then
ca analyze will look at the default binary.errlog and has the lastest 
and greatest new theory rules for ds20e, es40 etc in it ....


Thanks again,
Andy



